iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:154:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:155:## Bibliography Candidates
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:156:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:157:- Pooria Joulani, Andras Gyorgy, Csaba Szepesvari. “Online Learning under Delayed Feedback.” ICML 2013, PMLR 28(3):1453-1461. https://proceedings.mlr.press/v28/joulani13.html. Relevant for black-box delayed-feedback reductions; constant delay \(H\) yields the needed expert-style \(O(\sqrt{TH\log K})\) scaling.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:158:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:159:- Kent Quanrud, Daniel Khashabi. “Online Learning with Adversarial Delays.” NeurIPS 2015. https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2015/hash/72da7fd6d1302c0a159f6436d01e9eb0-Abstract.html. Relevant background for regret controlled by total delay.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:160:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:161:- Lukas Zierahn, Dirk van der Hoeven, Tal Lancewicki, Aviv Rosenberg, Nicolò Cesa-Bianchi. “A Unified Analysis of Nonstochastic Delayed Feedback for Combinatorial Semi-Bandits, Linear Bandits, and MDPs.” JMLR 26(104):1-60, 2025. https://www.jmlr.org/papers/v26/24-0496.html. Modern delayed-feedback reference; less directly needed because the truncated problem here is full-information.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:162:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:163:## Recommended Next Steps
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:164:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:165:Promote \(\gamma(h)\to0\) as a sufficient condition theorem.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:166:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:167:For necessity, first fix the intended quantifier. If process-specific, record the counterexample above and abandon necessity of uniform \(\gamma\). If class-uniform/minimax, try a two-process indistinguishability lower bound where delayed positive-payoff events hide which of two separated quotes is better.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:168:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/explorer_01.md:169:Also consider replacing uniform essential-sup \(\gamma\) by the ex-ante average tail \(\Delta_T(H)\), which is closer to what the truncation proof actually needs.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:1:# Payoff-Weighted Tail
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:2:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:3:ID: idea_02
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:4:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:5:## Summary
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:6:Replace beta by the payoff-weighted tail gamma(h)=sup_t sup_a esssup a Pr(h<tau_t(a)<infty | history). Prove the same upper bound with T gamma(H) in place of T beta(H), and show equivalence to uniform tightness over positive-scale actions a>=epsilon for every epsilon>0. Then test whether gamma(h)->0 is necessary or only sufficient.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:7:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:8:## Why Promising
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:9:It directly repairs the solver's obstruction: long delays at a=0 or tiny quote levels should not matter for regret.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:10:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:11:## Risks
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:12:The essential supremum over histories may still be too strong; rare histories or isolated times can violate gamma without causing linear expected regret.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:13:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:14:## Suggested Lenses
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:15:- proof strategy
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:16:- condition refinement
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/idea.md:17:- counterexample search
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:1:## Summary
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:2:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:3:No fatal gap in the explorer’s weighted-tail sufficiency proof, assuming the price process is exogenous and the truncated problem is treated as full-information delayed experts. The main theorem that survives is:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:4:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:5:\[
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:6:\gamma(h)\to 0 \implies R(T)=o(T)
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:7:\]
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:8:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:9:with the stated bound
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:10:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:11:\[
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:12:R(T)\le O(\sqrt{TH\log K})+\frac{T}{K}+T\gamma(H).
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:13:\]
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:14:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:15:The necessity claim does not survive without much sharper quantifiers. The explorer’s counterexample is a credible obstruction to process-specific necessity.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:16:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:17:## Issue List
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:18:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:19:- **Missing assumption:** The upper bound needs an explicit exogeneity/adaptivity condition. The delayed-expert reduction is valid if the full reward vector \(r_t^H(\cdot)\) is determined by the price path independently of the learner’s current random action. If future \(P_s\) can react to \(a_t\), this is no longer a standard delayed full-information problem.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:20:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:21:- **Missing assumption:** Replace `max` over \([0,1]\) by `sup`, or assume comparator existence. With strict trade \(a<P_t\), atoms can destroy maximizers. Example: if future prices are constantly \(1/2\), the payoff supremum is approached by \(a\uparrow 1/2\) but not attained.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:22:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:23:- **Plausible but incomplete:** The citation to delayed expert learning should be made theorem-level precise. Joulani-Gyorgy-Szepesvari and Quanrud-Khashabi support regret controlled by delays, but the writeup should state the exact full-information bounded-reward theorem being invoked and its convention for delay \(H\).
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:24:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:25:- **Worth pursuing:** Lemma 2, the equivalence
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:26:  \[
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:27:  \gamma(h)\to0 \Longleftrightarrow \forall \epsilon>0,\ \beta_\epsilon(h)\to0,
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:28:  \]
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:29:  appears correct. The proof is short and should be promoted.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:30:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:31:- **Plausible but incomplete:** The average-tail condition \(\Delta_T(H)\) is a good weaker sufficient condition, but it should be written horizon-indexedly:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:32:  \[
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:33:  \exists H(T):\quad H(T)\log T=o(T),\qquad \Delta_T(H(T))=o(T).
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:34:  \]
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:35:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:36:- **Missing assumption / quantifier gap:** “\(\gamma\not\to0\) is not necessary” is only established under process-specific learnability. For uniform minimax learnability over a class, the counterexample does not rule out a necessity-type lower bound.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:37:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:38:## Counterexamples Or Stress Tests
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:39:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:40:- **Max failure stress test:** Let \(P_t\equiv c\in(0,1)\). A fixed quote \(a<c\) eventually trades, while \(a\ge c\) does not. The best fixed payoff is approached as \(a\uparrow c\), but no maximizing \(a\) exists.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:41:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:42:- **Necessity stress test:** The explorer’s coded-delay construction is credible. Conditional on \(P_1=x_m\), a quote \(a=1/2\) has delayed trade probability \(1/2\) at arbitrarily large delays, so \(\gamma(h)\not\to0\). Yet all fixed-action expected rewards are scalar multiples of \(a(1-a)\), so always quoting \(1/2\) has zero regret. This breaks process-specific necessity.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:43:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:44:## Literature Or Known-Result Conflicts
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:45:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:46:No direct conflict found. The delayed-feedback literature supports the finite-arm delayed-learning component: Joulani, Gyorgy, and Szepesvari give black-box delayed-feedback reductions for online learning, and Quanrud-Khashabi give regret bounds in terms of total delay \(D\), consistent with \(D\lesssim TH\) yielding \(O(\sqrt{TH})\)-type scaling. See Joulani et al. ICML 2013 ([proceedings.mlr.press](https://proceedings.mlr.press/v28/joulani13.html)) and Quanrud-Khashabi NeurIPS 2015 ([proceedings.neurips.cc](https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2015/hash/72da7fd6d1302c0a159f6436d01e9eb0-Abstract.html)).
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:47:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:48:The Zierahn et al. JMLR 2025 / COLT 2023 line is relevant background for delayed bandit/structured feedback, but less directly necessary for this full-information truncated reduction ([jmlr.org](https://www.jmlr.org/papers/v26/24-0496.html)) ([proceedings.mlr.press](https://proceedings.mlr.press/v195/hoeven23a.html)).
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:49:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:50:## What Survives The Critique
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:51:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:52:- Weighted truncation lemma survives.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:53:- Positive-scale equivalence survives.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:54:- \(\gamma(h)\to0\) is a clean sufficient condition.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:55:- The average ex-ante weighted tail \(\Delta_T\) is likely the right refinement if the essential supremum is too strong.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:56:- Necessity should be abandoned or reformulated with explicit minimax/class-uniform quantifiers.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:57:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:58:## Bibliography Candidates
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:59:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:60:- Pooria Joulani, Andras Gyorgy, Csaba Szepesvari. “Online Learning under Delayed Feedback.” ICML 2013, PMLR 28(3):1453-1461. https://proceedings.mlr.press/v28/joulani13.html. Relevant for delayed-feedback reductions.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:61:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:62:- Kent Quanrud, Daniel Khashabi. “Online Learning with Adversarial Delays.” NeurIPS 2015. https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2015/hash/72da7fd6d1302c0a159f6436d01e9eb0-Abstract.html. Relevant for regret bounds controlled by total delay.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:63:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:64:- Lukas Zierahn, Dirk van der Hoeven, Tal Lancewicki, Aviv Rosenberg, Nicolò Cesa-Bianchi. “A Unified Analysis of Nonstochastic Delayed Feedback for Combinatorial Semi-Bandits, Linear Bandits, and MDPs.” JMLR 26(104):1-60, 2025; earlier COLT 2023 version. https://www.jmlr.org/papers/v26/24-0496.html. Background for modern delayed-feedback analysis.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:65:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:66:## Recommended Next Checks
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:67:
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:68:1. Formalize the theorem with `sup` regret and explicit exogenous price filtration.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:69:2. Write the exact delayed full-information lemma needed for \(K\) experts and delay at most \(H\).
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:70:3. Promote \(\gamma\to0\) as a sufficient condition, not an iff condition.
iterations/iter_001/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md:71:4. Decide whether the final “only if” target is process-specific or minimax over a class; these are different problems.

